Q6. What is the difference between method overloading and method overriding?
========================

ANSWER:

Method overloading occurs when multiple methods have the same name but different parameter lists within a class. It is compile-time polymorphism.

Method overriding occurs when a child class provides its own implementation of a method already defined in its parent class. It is runtime polymorphism.

For example:

add(int, int)
add(int, int, int)

demonstrate overloading.

A Dog class overriding the sound() method of Animal demonstrates overriding.


