Q12. What is the difference between ArrayList and LinkedList?
========================

ANSWER:

ArrayList internally uses a dynamic array, while LinkedList uses linked nodes.

ArrayList provides efficient random access with O(1) average access time, while LinkedList requires O(n) traversal for indexed access.

LinkedList can be more efficient for insertions and deletions when the node position is already known.

ArrayList is generally preferred for frequent random access.

Both maintain insertion order and allow duplicate elements.


