Q13. What is the difference between HashMap and HashSet?
========================

ANSWER:

HashMap stores data as key-value pairs, while HashSet stores unique elements.

HashMap does not allow duplicate keys but can contain duplicate values.

HashSet does not allow duplicate elements.

Both are hash-based collections and generally provide average O(1) time for basic operations such as insertion, search, and deletion.

We use HashMap when we need key-value mapping and HashSet when we need uniqueness.


