Q17. Explain binary search and its time complexity.
========================

ANSWER:

Binary search is an algorithm used to find a target element in a sorted collection.

We maintain left and right boundaries, calculate the middle element, and compare it with the target.

Depending on the comparison, we discard half of the search space and continue.

Because the search space is divided by two at every step:

Time Complexity = O(log n)

Iterative Space Complexity = O(1)


